invariant: INV-46
file: mlkem.c
catches: test/mlkem-builds.sh
reason: mlkem.c guards its call to the vector base multiplication on a
  macro no build defines, so a host object's sessions run
  mlkem_poly.c's loop. Every vector passes, because the loop computes
  the same coefficients, so the script compiles mlkem.c as a host object
  does and requires it to call mlk_vector_basemul and not
  mlk_poly_basemul.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    mlk_vector_basemul(r, a, b);
--- new
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME_PATH
    mlk_vector_basemul(r, a, b);
